# .dockerignore for `frontend/`'s build context -- resolves
# `problems_final_review.md` P2-12: `frontend/Dockerfile`'s builder
# stage does `COPY package.json package-lock.json ./` then `COPY . .`
# with build context `frontend/` (see that Dockerfile's own header
# comment: `docker build -t tdm-console:local frontend`). Without this
# file, a developer's local `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `test-results/`,
# coverage output, or `.env*` sitting in their `frontend/` checkout
# would be sent into the Docker build context -- not a secret-exposure
# risk here (nothing sensitive lives in any of these), but wasteful
# (`npm ci` inside the container reinstalls regardless) and not best
# practice.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
